      "content": "Research suggests that individuals from East Asian backgrounds often exhibit high levels of conscientiousness and a strong focus on group harmony, which can manifest as stoicism under pressure. In contrast, individuals from Mediterranean and Latin backgrounds may display higher levels of emotional expressiveness, often managing stress through strong social support networks and more overt emotional processing. These differences reflect cultural orientations regarding emotion, interdependence, and coping strategies rather than innate traits.",
