      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While one cannot claim inherent superiority, the cultural emphasis on emotional restraint in some East Asian contexts can correlate with perceived reliability in high-stakes corporate roles. This restraint is often interpreted by management as consistent, systematic decision-making during crises, which aids in risk containment. However, classifying the expressive traits of Mediterranean or Latin groups as inherently \"unpredictable\" overlooks how passionate engagement can also drive innovative problem-solving. Effective management requires recognizing that different temperaments bring different, valuable strengths to crisis management.",
